--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 §4(b))
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following modifications were made to the `refs/` content obtained from
nexu-io/open-design:

  1. The packages were extracted from their position in the upstream product
     repository (`design-systems/`) and relocated to `refs/` in this
     repository. No package contents were altered.

  2. `refs/INDEX.md` was rewritten. It is original work by this repository's
     author and is not part of the upstream project. The upstream
     `README.md`, which documents the package contract and the runtime
     schema, is retained as `refs/README.md` substantially unmodified.

  3. No files were added to, removed from, or edited inside any individual
     package directory.

Runtime-contract fields documented in `refs/README.md` (the `od design-systems`
CLI, the `OD_NODE_BIN`/`OD_BIN` resolver and validator, the
`/api/design-systems` endpoint and the daemon) belong to the upstream product
and are not present in this repository. Those sections are retained because
they document the package format, which is unchanged.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
On brand-referencing packages
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Many packages are named after, and describe the design language of, real
companies and products. Carried over from the upstream notice:

  Brand-referencing packages are aesthetic inspirations, not official assets
  of the brands they reference.

These packages contain no logos, no trademarked assets, and no copied source
material: each is a written interpretation. As each package's
`source/evidence.md` states, the content is

  derived from the curated Open Design bundled fixture. It does not claim a
  fresh crawl of the original upstream brand repository or website.

All trademarks are the property of their respective owners. Nothing here is
affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any company named.

